# Next.js Image Optimization

## Overview
Next.js provides the `next/image` component to automatically optimize images and prevent layout shifts (CLS - Cumulative Layout Shift).

## Key Concepts

### Why Images Cause Layout Shifts
- When images load without specified dimensions, the browser doesn't reserve space
- This causes content to jump when the image loads
- Negatively impacts Core Web Vitals (CLS score)

### Solution: next/image Component

```jsx
import Image from 'next/image'

// Fixed dimensions (recommended for known sizes)
<Image
  src="/product.jpg"
  width={500}
  height={300}
  alt="Product description"
/>

// Responsive with layout fill (for containers)
<div style={{ position: 'relative', width: '100%', height: '400px' }}>
  <Image
    src="/product.jpg"
    layout="fill"
    objectFit="cover"
    alt="Product description"
  />
</div>

// Priority loading for above-the-fold images
<Image
  src="/hero.jpg"
  width={1200}
  height={600}
  priority
  alt="Hero image"
/>
```

## Common Patterns

### Product Images in E-commerce
```jsx
<Image
  src={product.imageUrl}
  width={400}
  height={400}
  alt={product.name}
  placeholder="blur"
  blurDataURL="data:image/jpeg;base64,..."
/>
```

### Responsive Images
```jsx
<Image
  src="/banner.jpg"
  width={1200}
  height={400}
  layout="responsive"
  alt="Banner"
/>
```

## Migration from <img> to <Image>

### Before (causes layout shift)
```jsx
<img src="/product.jpg" alt="Product" />
```

### After (prevents layout shift)
```jsx
<Image src="/product.jpg" width={500} height={500} alt="Product" />
```

## Best Practices
1. Always specify width and height for fixed images
2. Use `priority` for above-the-fold images
3. Use `layout="fill"` for responsive containers
4. Add `alt` text for accessibility
5. Use `placeholder="blur"` for better UX
6. Configure image domains in next.config.js for external images

## Configuration

```js
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  images: {
    domains: ['example.com', 'cdn.example.com'],
    deviceSizes: [640, 750, 828, 1080, 1200, 1920, 2048, 3840],
    imageSizes: [16, 32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 256, 384],
  },
}
```
