# React Loading States Best Practices

## Overview
Proper loading states prevent layout shifts, improve perceived performance, and enhance user experience.

## Loading State Patterns

### Basic Loading State
```jsx
const ProductList = () => {
  const [products, setProducts] = useState([])
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchProducts()
      .then(setProducts)
      .finally(() => setLoading(false))
  }, [])

  if (loading) {
    return <LoadingSpinner />
  }

  return <div>{products.map(p => <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />)}</div>
}
```

### Skeleton Screens (Preferred)
```jsx
const ProductList = () => {
  const [products, setProducts] = useState([])
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchProducts()
      .then(setProducts)
      .finally(() => setLoading(false))
  }, [])

  return (
    <div className="product-grid">
      {loading
        ? Array(6).fill(0).map((_, i) => <ProductCardSkeleton key={i} />)
        : products.map(p => <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />)
      }
    </div>
  )
}

const ProductCardSkeleton = () => (
  <div className="product-card">
    <div className="skeleton skeleton-image" style={{ height: '200px' }} />
    <div className="skeleton skeleton-title" style={{ height: '24px', marginTop: '12px' }} />
    <div className="skeleton skeleton-price" style={{ height: '20px', width: '40%', marginTop: '8px' }} />
  </div>
)
```

### Progressive Loading
```jsx
const ProductPage = ({ productId }) => {
  const [product, setProduct] = useState(null)
  const [reviews, setReviews] = useState(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    // Load product first (critical)
    fetchProduct(productId).then(setProduct)

    // Load reviews after (non-critical)
    fetchReviews(productId).then(setReviews)
  }, [productId])

  return (
    <div>
      {product ? (
        <ProductDetails product={product} />
      ) : (
        <ProductDetailsSkeleton />
      )}

      <div style={{ minHeight: '300px' }}>
        {reviews ? (
          <ReviewsList reviews={reviews} />
        ) : (
          <ReviewsSkeleton />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Suspense (React 18+)
```jsx
import { Suspense } from 'react'

const ProductPage = () => {
  return (
    <div>
      <Suspense fallback={<ProductDetailsSkeleton />}>
        <ProductDetails />
      </Suspense>

      <Suspense fallback={<ReviewsSkeleton />}>
        <Reviews />
      </Suspense>
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Error States
```jsx
const ProductList = () => {
  const [products, setProducts] = useState([])
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)
  const [error, setError] = useState(null)

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchProducts()
      .then(setProducts)
      .catch(setError)
      .finally(() => setLoading(false))
  }, [])

  if (error) {
    return <ErrorMessage error={error} retry={() => window.location.reload()} />
  }

  if (loading) {
    return <ProductListSkeleton />
  }

  return <div>{products.map(p => <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />)}</div>
}
```

## Custom Hooks for Loading
```jsx
const useAsync = (asyncFunction, immediate = true) => {
  const [status, setStatus] = useState('idle')
  const [data, setData] = useState(null)
  const [error, setError] = useState(null)

  const execute = useCallback(() => {
    setStatus('pending')
    setData(null)
    setError(null)

    return asyncFunction()
      .then(response => {
        setData(response)
        setStatus('success')
      })
      .catch(error => {
        setError(error)
        setStatus('error')
      })
  }, [asyncFunction])

  useEffect(() => {
    if (immediate) {
      execute()
    }
  }, [execute, immediate])

  return { execute, status, data, error }
}

// Usage
const ProductList = () => {
  const { status, data: products, error } = useAsync(fetchProducts)

  if (status === 'error') return <ErrorMessage error={error} />
  if (status === 'pending') return <ProductListSkeleton />
  if (status === 'success') return <div>{products.map(p => <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />)}</div>
}
```

## Skeleton Component Library
```jsx
const Skeleton = ({ width, height, className = '' }) => (
  <div
    className={`skeleton ${className}`}
    style={{
      width: width || '100%',
      height: height || '20px',
      backgroundColor: '#e0e0e0',
      borderRadius: '4px',
      animation: 'pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite',
    }}
  />
)

const SkeletonText = ({ lines = 3 }) => (
  <div>
    {Array(lines).fill(0).map((_, i) => (
      <Skeleton
        key={i}
        height="16px"
        width={i === lines - 1 ? '60%' : '100%'}
        style={{ marginBottom: '8px' }}
      />
    ))}
  </div>
)
```

## Best Practices
1. Always show loading states - never leave users wondering
2. Use skeleton screens instead of spinners for better UX
3. Match skeleton dimensions to actual content
4. Load critical content first, defer non-critical
5. Handle error states gracefully
6. Provide retry mechanisms for failed requests
7. Use Suspense for better code organization (React 18+)
8. Avoid layout shifts by reserving space
9. Show progressive loading for multiple data sources
10. Test loading states in development

